<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />

    <!-- Theme bootstrap - see the matching comment in base.html. Blocking on
         purpose so [data-theme] and [data-color-scheme] exist before first
         paint. Mirrors loadSavedTheme() in theme-switcher.ts; keep in sync. -->
    <script>
      (function () {
        var d = document.documentElement;
        try {
          d.setAttribute(
            "data-theme",
            localStorage.getItem("kbr-theme") || "base"
          );
          d.setAttribute(
            "data-color-scheme",
            localStorage.getItem("kbr-color-scheme") ||
              (window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches
                ? "dark"
                : "light")
          );
        } catch (e) {
          d.setAttribute("data-theme", "base");
          d.setAttribute("data-color-scheme", "light");
        }
      })();
    </script>

    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>Intentional Work Patterns</title>
    
    <meta name="description" content="Build intentional habits to prevent chaos from controlling your work or seeping into your personal life" />
     
    <meta name="keywords" content="habits, intentionality, remote work" />
     
      <link rel="stylesheet" crossorigin href="/assets/index-HASH.css">
</head>

  <body>
    <kbr-navigation>
      <!-- Slotted into .header-content so the switcher sits at the far right
           of the site header. It used to be a fixed-position floating control,
           which overlapped page content at every viewport width. See DF-31. -->
      <kbr-theme-switcher slot="theme-switcher"></kbr-theme-switcher>
    </kbr-navigation>

    <main class="blog-post-layout">
      <aside class="blog-toc-sidebar">
        <div class="blog-toc-sticky-container">
          
          <kbr-post-series
            series-name="Intentional Work Patterns"
            current-part="0"
          >
          </kbr-post-series>
          
          <kbr-table-of-contents></kbr-table-of-contents>
           
      <div class="blog-post-tags">
        <span class="tags-label">Tags:</span>
        <div class="tag-list">
          <button class="blog-tag" data-tag="habits">habits</button><button class="blog-tag" data-tag="intentionality">intentionality</button><button class="blog-tag" data-tag="remote work">remote work</button>
        </div>
      </div>
     
        </div>
      </aside>

      <article class="blog-post-content glass-surface">
        <h1 id="intentional-work-patterns">Intentional Work Patterns</h1>

        <div class="blog-post-metadata">
          <div>
            <time datetime="2025-12-26">December 26, 2025</time>
          </div>
        </div>
      <p>Remote work offers flexibility, but without intentional structure, work can easily bleed into personal time. And personal distractions can fragment your workday. This series shares the specific habits and patterns I&#39;ve developed to maintain both productivity and work-life balance.</p>
<p>While these patterns emerged from remote work, many of them apply to any work environment.</p>
<ol>
<li><a href="/intentional-work-patterns-boundaries.html">Setting boundaries</a>: Practical strategies for protecting your time and energy</li>
<li>Remote work traps: Common patterns that derail remote workers</li>
<li>Work rituals: How start-of-day and end-of-day routines reinforce boundaries</li>
<li>Physical and digital spaces: Creating environments that support focus</li>
<li>Building connections: Staying visible and connected in distributed teams</li>
</ol>
<p>If you are looking for practical implementation details, see the companion supplements below.</p>

        <kbr-supplement-list></kbr-supplement-list>
        

        <kbr-anchor-copy></kbr-anchor-copy>
      </article>
    </main>

    <!-- Shared markup from templates/partials/footer.html, injected by
         template-processor.ts. Edit the partial, not this line. -->
    <!--
  Shared site footer.

  This is the single source of the footer markup. It is injected into both
  base.html and blog-post.html as the {&lt;!--
  Shared site footer.

  This is the single source of the footer markup. It is injected into both
  base.html and blog-post.html as the  template variable, wired up
  in source/builder/template-processor.ts - which is the one choke point both
  the production build and the dev server render through. Do not paste this
  markup into a template; add the variable instead, or every page type grows
  its own copy.

  Light DOM on purpose, not a Lit component: the footer has to be present in
  the generated HTML for crawlers and for readers without JavaScript, and a
  shadow root would leave only an empty custom element in the static output.
--&gt;
&lt;footer class=&quot;site-footer&quot;&gt;
  &lt;nav class=&quot;site-footer-nav&quot; aria-label=&quot;Elsewhere on the web&quot;&gt;
    &lt;ul&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;a
          href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/in/kyle-blank-rollins/&quot;
          target=&quot;_blank&quot;
          rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;
          &gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a
        &gt;
      &lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;a
          href=&quot;https://github.com/KyleBlankRollins/Web-Portfolio&quot;
          target=&quot;_blank&quot;
          rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;
          &gt;GitHub&lt;/a
        &gt;
      &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;/ul&gt;
  &lt;/nav&gt;
&lt;/footer&gt;} template variable, wired up
  in source/builder/template-processor.ts - which is the one choke point both
  the production build and the dev server render through. Do not paste this
  markup into a template; add the variable instead, or every page type grows
  its own copy.

  Light DOM on purpose, not a Lit component: the footer has to be present in
  the generated HTML for crawlers and for readers without JavaScript, and a
  shadow root would leave only an empty custom element in the static output.
-->
<footer class="site-footer">
  <nav class="site-footer-nav" aria-label="Elsewhere on the web">
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kyle-blank-rollins/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >LinkedIn</a
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/KyleBlankRollins/Web-Portfolio"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >GitHub</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
  </nav>
</footer>
      <script type="module" crossorigin src="/assets/index-HASH.js"></script>
    <script type="module" crossorigin src="/assets/lit-HASH.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
